## Overview
Upload a client requirements PDF → generate: project scope, timeline, quote, contract draft, discovery questions.

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 (App Router, TypeScript)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- **AI**: `@anthropic-ai/sdk` — default model `claude-opus-4-8`
- **PDF parsing**: `pdf-parse` (server-side text extraction)
- **Export**: `@react-pdf/renderer`
- **Package manager**: `npm`

## Project Structure
```
src/
  app/
    api/generate/   # Streaming AI generation endpoint
    page.tsx        # Upload + proposal UI
  components/       # UploadZone, ProposalSection, ExportButton
  lib/
    claude.ts       # Anthropic client + streaming helper
    pdf.ts          # PDF extraction wrapper
    prompts.ts      # ALL prompt templates — never inline elsewhere
  types/index.ts    # ProposalOutput, Section types
```

## Commands
- `npm run dev` — localhost:3000
- `npm run build` — production build
- `npm run typecheck` — `tsc --noEmit`
- `npm run lint` — ESLint

## Core Data Flow
1. User uploads PDF (max 10 MB, enforced client-side)
2. `/api/generate` extracts text via `pdf-parse`, validates it's non-empty
3. Streams prompt to Claude → returns JSON: `scope`, `timeline`, `quote`, `contract`, `questions`
4. UI renders each section independently; user copies or exports as PDF

## Architecture Decisions (MVP)
- No database — generate and display/export in-session; add persistence only when explicitly requested
- One API route (`/api/generate`) for all sections; split only if latency becomes a measured problem
